---- integer and float division semantics
ok   floor_divide on negative ints equals Python // (floor)
ok   remainder / mod on negative ints "has the same sign as the divisor" (equals Python %)
ok   fmod on negative ints "has the same sign as the dividend" (equals C fmod)
ok   divmod on ints equals Python divmod
ok   floor_divide / remainder on int arrays: [-7//2, 7//-2, -7//-2, 7//2] and remainders
ok   int8: floor_divide / remainder equal Python semantics
ok   uint8: floor_divide / remainder equal Python semantics
ok   int32: floor_divide / remainder equal Python semantics
ok   floor_divide on floats equals Python // including the sign of zero results
ok   remainder on floats equals Python % including the sign of zero results (remainder(-0.0, 3.0) = +0.0)
ok   fmod on floats equals math.fmod including signed zeros (fmod(-0.0, 3.0) = -0.0)
ok   divmod on floats equals Python divmod
ok   floor_divide and remainder satisfy "a = a % b + b * (a // b)" up to roundoff
   int array // 0 -> [0, 0, 0] warnings ['RuntimeWarning'] ['divide by zero encountered in floor_divide']
ok   int array floor_divide by 0 returns 0 with a RuntimeWarning (divide by zero)
ok   int remainder by 0 "Returns 0 when x2 is 0 and both x1 and x2 are integers" (with a warning)  (warnings ['RuntimeWarning'])
ok   int fmod by 0 returns 0 (recorded) with a warning  (got [0, 0], warnings ['RuntimeWarning'])
ok   int divmod by 0 returns (0, 0) with a warning  (warnings ['RuntimeWarning'])
ok   np.int64(7) // np.int64(0) returns 0 with a RuntimeWarning (no ZeroDivisionError, unlike Python)  (warnings ['RuntimeWarning'])
   int array / 0 -> [inf, -inf, nan] dtype float64 warnings ['RuntimeWarning']
ok   int array / 0 -> [inf, -inf, nan] float64 with RuntimeWarnings (divide, invalid)
ok   errstate(divide='raise'): int array // 0 raises FloatingPointError
   1/0, -1/0, 0/0, 1/-0.0 = [inf, -inf, nan, -inf] warnings ['RuntimeWarning'] ['divide by zero encountered in divide', 'invalid value encountered in divide']
ok   float division by zero follows IEEE: 1/0=inf, -1/0=-inf, 0/0=nan, 1/-0.0=-inf, with RuntimeWarnings
   1.0//0.0, 1.0%0.0, fmod(1,0), -1.0//0.0, 0.0//0.0 = [inf, nan, nan, -inf, nan] warnings ['divide by zero encountered in floor_divide', 'invalid value encountered in floor_divide', 'invalid value encountered in fmod', 'invalid value encountered in remainder']
ok   float floor_divide by 0.0 -> inf / -inf / nan (IEEE, recorded), remainder and fmod by 0.0 -> nan, with warnings
ok   negative(0.0) = -0.0, 0.0 * -1 = -0.0, sqrt(-0.0) = -0.0 (IEEE), -0.0 + 0.0 = +0.0
ok   abs(-0.0) = +0.0 and -0.0 == 0.0 compares equal
ok   np.round(-0.4) = -0.0, np.sign(-0.0) = 0.0 with signbit(sign(-0.0)) recorded  (signbit(sign(-0.0)) = False)
